OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 21 MAY
OL,4,G2145FThe Essay: Full Moon on Progress
OL,5,     FSt
OL,6,     GDr Rommi Smith examines a key
OL,7,     Gmoment in the life and work of
OL,8,     Gfive Black female musicians.
OL,9,     GToday she considers the political
OL,10,     Gawakening of Nina Simone.
OL,11,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,12,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,13,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,14,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,15,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,16,     Geverything in between.
OL,17,G2330F'Round Midnight
OL,18,     GJas Kayser, in for Soweto Kinch,
OL,19,     Gpresents another hour of the best
OL,20,     Gin jazz, and Louis Hayes returns
OL,21,     Gwith his fourth selection of the
OL,22,     Gweek.
